From: SinCuri0 <SinCuri0@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] vulkan: keep task and mesh pipelines on disk, in a file of their own (EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE)

Core patch, for tools/eglantine-patches after pipeline-keep-01.

Port of the mesh half of zortos293/Lichii PR 192 (open, not merged), SinCuri0, branch
disk-cache-mesh-pipelines, commit b8e8e0a5c058d1dc5bf2465794ecc4eb907ed7d4. GPL-3.0, as this tree.

CreateGraphicsPipeline() returned before SerializePipeline for a mesh pipeline, and the loader
dropped any it found, because the entry format has no mesh registers. So each session built them
again, whatever was saved. The environments now also write mesh_registers and
mesh_primitive_header, the two values translation reads from the live registers.

Use this once mesh draws run (real ones, or fable-mesh-compute-0181). While they are skipped,
EDEN_NX2_NO_MESH_BUILD is better: this only moves the work to boot, the pipelines are still built.
With both set, the file is left alone.

Changed from the source:
- A switch: EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE=1. Default off: nothing is written or read, as before.
- Own file, vulkan_mesh.bin, instead of new entries in vulkan.bin. The PR keeps the cache version
  and reads the two values for every task or mesh entry. An entry written before they were left
  out has no such values, and the loader's old comment says those can exist. The PS5's reader
  (headless/shader_cache_reader.inc, which replaces LoadPipelines) takes that for damage and cuts
  the file back: in a test, made-up entries, a 1436-byte vulkan.bin with one stale entry lost it and
  all that followed, 424 bytes left. Core's LoadPipelines was seen to throw std::bad_alloc there,
  which it does not catch, and to spin for over a minute without the change on a file with mesh
  entries (once each, made-up data; not the PS5's path). With an own file none of this can touch
  vulkan.bin, a build without this patch never opens it, and a damaged one takes only itself with
  it. CACHE_VERSION is unchanged.
- FileEnvironment::read_mesh_fields tells Deserialize which file it reads, set around the second
  load. Not a LoadPipelines argument: the PS5 build compiles its own LoadPipelines, which calls
  Deserialize(file), so a new argument leaves the call without a definition at link, and without
  the values the reader cuts vulkan_mesh.bin back to its header every boot.
- The trap prefix half of the PR is left out: this tree has no trap_prefix and CanBeSerialized never
  refused those programs.

Test results, on the Mac, real shader_environment.cpp, made-up entries, both the PS5 reader and
core's: an old file with a stale mesh entry reads through with the flag off and is not cut; task,
mesh, registers, primitive header and key come back from vulkan_mesh.bin unchanged, not cut. PS5
reader only: a cut tail keeps the whole entries before it. Plain entries are untouched by the diff.
GenericEnvironment::Serialize writes the new values for every task or mesh entry, but only this path
stores any: OpenGL throws on those programs.

The PR's table is from an RTX 5070 Ti; its numbers do not carry over.

Memory: mesh pipelines used in the last two sessions are built at boot. Not run on a console.
Syntax checked with clang (stubs for the SDK).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
index fb6f0fdb27..cf367887f8 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.cpp
@@ -694,6 +694,18 @@ bool PreloadAllPipelines() {
     }();
     return all;
 }
+
+// EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE=1 keeps task and mesh pipelines in <title>/vulkan_mesh.bin, so that a
+// session builds them at boot like the rest. Off, they are built on the GPU thread every session.
+// Their own file, not vulkan.bin: an entry there has the mesh registers, an entry from before task
+// and mesh pipelines were left out does not, and the two cannot be told apart while reading.
+bool MeshDiskCache() {
+    static const bool enabled = [] {
+        const char* value = std::getenv("EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE");
+        return value != nullptr && value[0] == '1';
+    }();
+    return enabled;
+}
 } // Anonymous namespace
 
 bool DropMeshDrawsBeforeBuild() {
@@ -818,6 +830,9 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
     }
     pipeline_cache_filename = base_dir / "vulkan.bin";
     used_pipelines_filename = base_dir / "vulkan_used.bin";
+    if (MeshDiskCache() && !DropMeshDrawsBeforeBuild()) {
+        mesh_pipeline_cache_filename = base_dir / "vulkan_mesh.bin";
+    }
     used_pipelines = LoadUsedPipelines(used_pipelines_filename, MaxUsedPipelineAge(device));
     used_pipelines_saved = std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
     size_t skipped_pipelines = 0;
@@ -858,13 +873,14 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
         });
         ++state.total;
     }};
+    bool reading_mesh_file = false;
     const auto load_graphics{[&](std::ifstream& file, std::vector<FileEnvironment> envs) {
         GraphicsPipelineCacheKey key;
         file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&key), sizeof(key));
 
-        // Task/mesh pipelines are not stored (their mesh registers are not in the format); skip
-        // any that were.
-        if (std::ranges::any_of(envs, [](const FileEnvironment& env) {
+        // Task/mesh pipelines are not stored in vulkan.bin (their mesh registers are not in its
+        // format, see MeshDiskCache); skip any that were.
+        if (!reading_mesh_file && std::ranges::any_of(envs, [](const FileEnvironment& env) {
                 return env.ShaderStage() == Shader::Stage::Task ||
                        env.ShaderStage() == Shader::Stage::Mesh;
             })) {
@@ -931,6 +947,15 @@ void PipelineCache::LoadDiskResources(u64 title_id, std::stop_token stop_loading
     }};
     VideoCommon::LoadPipelines(stop_loading, pipeline_cache_filename, CACHE_VERSION, load_compute,
                                load_graphics);
+    if (!mesh_pipeline_cache_filename.empty()) {
+        reading_mesh_file = true;
+        FileEnvironment::read_mesh_fields = true;
+        SCOPE_EXIT {
+            FileEnvironment::read_mesh_fields = false;
+        };
+        VideoCommon::LoadPipelines(stop_loading, mesh_pipeline_cache_filename, CACHE_VERSION,
+                                   load_compute, load_graphics);
+    }
 
     LOG_INFO(Render_Vulkan, "Total Pipeline Count: {}", state.total);
     if (skipped_pipelines != 0) {
@@ -1443,10 +1468,14 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
     if (!pipeline || pipeline_cache_filename.empty()) {
         return pipeline;
     }
-    if (pipeline->IsMeshPipeline()) {
+    const bool is_mesh{pipeline->IsMeshPipeline()};
+    if (is_mesh) {
         reason = RuntimeBuild::Mesh;
-        // Not stored: task and mesh programs are translated with the mesh registers, which the
-        // cache format does not carry. The few of them rebuild quickly from the driver cache.
+    }
+    if (is_mesh && mesh_pipeline_cache_filename.empty()) {
+        // Not stored: task and mesh programs are translated with the mesh registers, which
+        // vulkan.bin does not carry. They are built again on this thread every session, driver
+        // cache or not (EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE).
         QueueVulkanPipelineCacheFlush();
         return pipeline;
     }
@@ -1456,7 +1485,8 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
         return pipeline;
     }
     disk_pipelines.insert(graphics_key.Hash());
-    serialization_thread.QueueWork([this, key = graphics_key, envs = std::move(environments.envs)] {
+    serialization_thread.QueueWork([this, is_mesh, key = graphics_key,
+                                    envs = std::move(environments.envs)] {
         try {
             boost::container::static_vector<const GenericEnvironment*, Maxwell::MaxShaderProgram>
                 env_ptrs;
@@ -1465,7 +1495,9 @@ std::unique_ptr<GraphicsPipeline> PipelineCache::CreateGraphicsPipeline() {
                     env_ptrs.push_back(&envs[index]);
                 }
             }
-            SerializePipeline(key, env_ptrs, pipeline_cache_filename, CACHE_VERSION);
+            SerializePipeline(key, env_ptrs,
+                              is_mesh ? mesh_pipeline_cache_filename : pipeline_cache_filename,
+                              CACHE_VERSION);
         } catch (const std::bad_alloc&) {
             SurviveBadAlloc("a graphics pipeline's disk cache entry");
         }
diff --git a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
index 8938d4b50f..df63fd65de 100644
--- a/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
+++ b/src/video_core/renderer_vulkan/vk_pipeline_cache.h
@@ -203,6 +203,7 @@ private:
     Shader::HostTranslateInfo host_info;
 
     std::filesystem::path pipeline_cache_filename;
+    std::filesystem::path mesh_pipeline_cache_filename; ///< Empty unless EDEN_NX2_MESH_DISK_CACHE=1
 
     /// Key hashes of the graphics pipelines in the disk cache. Only those a recent session used
     /// (used_pipelines) are built at boot; the rest are built when first needed, and not stored
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp b/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
index 7969939e6e..c1233232cb 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_environment.cpp
@@ -326,6 +326,13 @@ void GenericEnvironment::Serialize(std::ofstream& file) const {
             file.write(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&gp_passthrough_mask),
                        sizeof(gp_passthrough_mask));
         }
+        // Only vulkan_mesh.bin holds task and mesh programs; FileEnvironment::Deserialize reads
+        // this with read_mesh_fields set.
+        if (stage == Shader::Stage::Task || stage == Shader::Stage::Mesh) {
+            file.write(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&mesh_registers), sizeof(mesh_registers))
+                .write(reinterpret_cast<const char*>(&mesh_primitive_header),
+                       sizeof(mesh_primitive_header));
+        }
     }
 }
 
@@ -909,6 +916,12 @@ void FileEnvironment::Deserialize(std::ifstream& file) {
         if (stage == Shader::Stage::Geometry) {
             file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&gp_passthrough_mask), sizeof(gp_passthrough_mask));
         }
+        if (read_mesh_fields &&
+            (stage == Shader::Stage::Task || stage == Shader::Stage::Mesh)) {
+            file.read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&mesh_registers), sizeof(mesh_registers))
+                .read(reinterpret_cast<char*>(&mesh_primitive_header),
+                      sizeof(mesh_primitive_header));
+        }
     }
     // Native programs fold bank 1 reads as they did when they were built.
     is_proprietary_driver = texture_bound == 2 || Shader::Ampere::HasNativeAddressMap(code);
diff --git a/src/video_core/shader_environment.h b/src/video_core/shader_environment.h
index f1f9398fcb..af7fe8133f 100644
--- a/src/video_core/shader_environment.h
+++ b/src/video_core/shader_environment.h
@@ -214,6 +214,11 @@ public:
 
     void Deserialize(std::ifstream& file);
 
+    /// True while this thread reads vulkan_mesh.bin, whose task and mesh programs carry their mesh
+    /// registers. Not an argument of LoadPipelines: the PS5 port compiles its own LoadPipelines
+    /// (headless/shader_cache_reader.inc), which calls Deserialize(file).
+    static inline thread_local bool read_mesh_fields{};
+
     [[nodiscard]] u64 ReadInstruction(u32 address) override;
 
     [[nodiscard]] u32 TranslateProgramAddress(u32 address) const override;
